{"conditionalSetIds":[],"forecasterId":"demographics-ai-2036:run1:growth:inside","informationSetArtifactId":"sha256:e4fe4e1dfdf3629dfebb5e2612b84002382be3044c52134575bf03c63c1226ab","modelForecastIds":[],"modelUse":"none","prediction":{"kind":"binary","positiveOutcomeId":"yes","probability":0.22},"questionHash":"sha256:cfe468fa9439bedeee3804a35583667745f13831322e2c91a89c02a1b211413b","questionId":"demographics-ai-2036-cq5","questionVersion":"1.0.0","rationale":"Conjunct 1 (MOVE average >= 105 over 2027-2036): marginal 45%. Mechanism, no base rate: MOVE is a price of rate-uncertainty insurance, and its structural floor is set by (i) duration supply per unit of risk-bearing capacity and (ii) who holds the marginal Treasury. Both are observed to be deteriorating — debt past 100% of GDP, net interest to 3%, and levered hedge-fund basis-trade absorption replacing price-insensitive official and bank demand. Levered intermediation makes the vol process jumpy: each deleveraging episode spikes MOVE to 140-160, and the quiet-year floor rises from ~65 (the 2010s, when a central bank was the marginal buyer) to ~85-95. A 10-year average of >= 105 therefore needs roughly three stress years out of ten given a ~90 floor. That is close to a coin flip and slightly under: 45%. Conjunct 2 (one episode with MSCI World -25% peak-to-trough while G7 10y nominal fails to fall >= 50 bp, or rises >= 25 bp): marginal 26%, built as two terms. P(MSCI World >= -25% drawdown at some point in 2027-2036) = 70%, derived mechanically rather than frequentially: the AI complex is plausibly ~33-38% of MSCI World capitalization by 2029-2030, and AI-Q4 (observed, 66%) is essentially the condition for that complex to de-rate 40-50%, which alone contributes 14-18 pp of index drawdown before any multiplier through private credit, the $650B debt stack and the wealth-effect channel. Then P(the flight-to-quality bid FAILS | that drawdown) = 37%. The bid fails only in three identifiable states: an inflation/supply-driven shock (the correlation mechanism: when the inflation-innovation share of macro-shock variance exceeds roughly 50%, stock-bond correlation flips from about -0.3 to +0.4); a sovereign-credibility shock where the Treasury IS the source; or forced cross-asset deleveraging where the basis trade unwinds and dealers sell duration into the equity decline. Crucially, the MODAL path for an AI-capex bust is DISINFLATIONARY, so bonds rally and conjunct 2 fails — this is the key mechanical reason I am well below where intuition puts this question. 0.70 x 0.37 = 0.26. Correlation: high and positive, rho = +0.55, because the levered-intermediation mechanism that lifts average MOVE is the same one that breaks the correlation regime. Joint = 0.45 x 0.26 + 0.55 x sqrt(0.2475 x 0.1924) = 0.117 + 0.120 = 0.237 -> 22.","referenceClassIds":[],"schemaVersion":"forecast-workbench.forecast/v1","sealedAt":"2026-11-04T17:31:54.314Z","seriesId":"published-panel","strongestContraryCase":"Not elicited per question. Panelist falsification signposts: {\"signpost\":\"OECD-38 health and social care job vacancy rate (Eurostat JVS + US JOLTS health care & social assistance), 4-quarter average, versus its 2025 level\",\"by_when\":\"Q4 2028\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"If care vacancy rates have FALLEN >= 25% from 2025 without an accompanying recession, my licensed-care-hours weakest link is wrong: raises CQ1 conjunct 1, raises CQ3 P50 by ~+0.15 pp, and shifts ~4 pp of CQ6 mass from C into A/B. If instead they have RISEN >= 20%, my CQ1 falls to ~12 (rationing confirmed as the clearing mechanism) and C rises ~3 pp.\"} | {\"signpost\":\"Median US FERC/ISO plus EU TSO interconnection queue wait for >100 MW load, paired with a real wage index for licensed high-voltage electricians and linemen (BLS 47-2111/49-9051 and Eurostat equivalents)\",\"by_when\":\"Dec 2029\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"If lineman/electrician real wages have risen < 10% cumulative 2025-2029 WHILE datacenter load has grown > 40%,